  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Possession 4 v 4 + 2 jokers",
  "description": "Mark a zone across the ice, from board to board and about 35–40 metres long, with a cone by the boards in each corner. Two teams of four play inside the zone. Two jokers stand outside the zone, one at each end of the zone, and always play with the team that has the ball, making it 6 v 4. The jokers may skate sideways behind their cone line but not into the zone. The team in possession scores a point for six passes in a row. Jokers get two touches and may not pass to each other. The boards are in play: a pass off the boards counts.\n\nIf the other team wins the ball, it is straight away their turn to count. Change jokers after a few minutes. If it gets too easy, make the zone shorter. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Create width and depth – use the ice from board to board and never stand two on the same line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use a joker or the boards to escape pressure, then switch play to the other side."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "When you lose the ball: press at once, the first seconds decide it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When you win it: first pass away from the pressure, ideally to a joker."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
